nd Characters 5-6-7. My hand lacks coordination, but I can aim for simple patterns like All Chows or Seat Wind.\n\nEvaluation: Key discards considered: T9 (dangerous, feeds across player's meld), W1/W3 (potential [W1,W2,W3] chow), W8/W9 (potential [W7,W8,W9]), B4 (spare tile, could be used for Kong), F3/B8 (pairs worth keeping). B1 stands out as having no meaningful use, as it cannot form a chow with existing tiles.\n\nReason: B1 cannot contribute to any chow due to lack of B2 and the use of B3 in an existing meld. Retaining it offers no strategic benefit, while discarding it avoids clutter and reduces risk of holding a useless terminal.\n\nAnswer: Play B1"}
